@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Docker Swarm (Orchestration)";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">
        Docker Swarm is Docker's built-in container orchestration tool. It enables clustering of Docker engines,
        allowing containers to be deployed and managed across multiple nodes seamlessly.
    </p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Section: Introduction to Docker Swarm -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Introduction to Docker Swarm</h2>
        <p>
            A Swarm is a group of Docker hosts (nodes) running in cluster mode.
            One or more manager nodes handle orchestration, while worker nodes execute containers.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Built directly into Docker Engine</li>
            <li>Supports service discovery and load balancing</li>
            <li>Enables high availability and failover</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Setting Up a Swarm Cluster -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Setting Up a Swarm Cluster</h3>
        <p>Initialize the Swarm on the manager node:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker swarm init</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>Add worker nodes using the generated token:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker swarm join --token &lt;worker-token&gt; &lt;manager-ip&gt;:2377</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>List all nodes in the Swarm:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker node ls</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Deploying Services -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Deploying Services in Swarm</h3>
        <p>Use the <code>docker service</code> command to deploy containers as Swarm services:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker service create --name web --replicas 3 -p 80:80 nginx</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>This runs 3 replicas of an NGINX container load-balanced across the cluster.</p>
        <p>Check running services:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker service ls</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>Inspect a specific service:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker service ps web</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Scaling Services -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Scaling Containers</h3>
        <p>Change the number of replicas dynamically:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker service scale web=5</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>This command increases the number of running containers from 3 to 5.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Rolling Updates and Rollbacks -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Rolling Updates & Rollbacks</h3>
        <p>Update the image version with zero downtime:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker service update --image nginx:1.25 web</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>To rollback in case of a failure:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker service rollback web</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Summary -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>
            Docker Swarm makes it easy to orchestrate container workloads with built-in clustering, load balancing, scaling, and self-healing.
            It’s a great choice for simpler, lightweight orchestration needs before moving to Kubernetes.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation Buttons -->
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("DockerSecurity", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
            &larr; Previous: Docker Security
        </a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("KubernetesVsDockerSwarm", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
            Next: Kubernetes vs. Docker Swarm &rarr;
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Copy Button Script -->
<script>
    document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach(btn => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
            const codeText = this.parentElement.querySelector('code')?.innerText;
            if (codeText) {
                navigator.clipboard.writeText(codeText).then(() => {
                    alert('Code copied to clipboard!');
                });
            }
        });
    });
</script>
